WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.600
When Kumail Nanjiani was cast in Marvel's&nbsp;
Eternals, he was determined to step up his game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.480
to play the samurai Kingo Sunen and challenged&nbsp;
himself to look the part. Here are the secrets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:14.720
the star and his personal trainer Grant Roberts&nbsp;
have revealed behind his bulking up journey.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.920
After seeing Kumail Nanjiani's photos of his&nbsp;
physical transformation, plenty of people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:24.080
wondered how he got those incredible results&nbsp;
— and if they could potentially recreate his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.920
success on their own. However, Nanjiani&nbsp;
has been open about the fact that his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.920
results would not have been possible if he&nbsp;
wasn't in a position of immense privilege.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.880
He worked with personal trainers and&nbsp;
nutritionists throughout the year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.880
all of whom were focused on creating&nbsp;
a custom program for his body, goals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.840
and lifestyle. Nanjiani wrote&nbsp;
in his Instagram caption,

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.000
"I would not have been able to do this if I&nbsp;
didn't have a full year with the best trainers and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.120
nutritionists paid for by the biggest studio in&nbsp;
the world. I'm glad I look like this, but I also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:55.920
understand why I never did before. It would have&nbsp;
been impossible without these resources and time."

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.800
Over the course of his fitness journey,&nbsp;
Kumail Nanjiani worked with many top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.640
personal trainers and nutritionists, all&nbsp;
of whom played an important role in helping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:08.640
him achieve his goals. But he spent most&nbsp;
of his time training with Grant Roberts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.800
who has also worked as an actor — you might&nbsp;
have spotted him in Sully, or in films like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:16.720
Million Dollar Baby. Being in front of the&nbsp;
camera himself meant that he understood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:22.480
exactly what Nanjiani needed to do in order to&nbsp;
prepare for Eternals. Roberts told Page Six,

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:27.120
"My process is completely individualized and&nbsp;
starts with the gathering of information.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:33.120
Current lifestyle, body composition tests, etc. I&nbsp;
also have a 3D scanner that's particularly useful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:36.720
for goal setting [...] and strategizing&nbsp;
the nutrition and training program."

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:41.520
The 3D body scanner that Roberts uses probably&nbsp;
doesn't come cheap, but these machines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:46.320
create accurate pictures of his client's body&nbsp;
composition, posture, and how their measurements&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.800
change as they work out. It was an invaluable&nbsp;
tool for creating Nanjiani's training program.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.800
"He scares me. Me too. But&nbsp;
he's an excellent motivator."

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.160
So, if you want to get muscles like Nanjiani,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.960
how often do you have to hit the gym? Nanjiani&nbsp;
generally worked out for a little over an hour,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.640
four to five days a week. However,&nbsp;
recovery time was an important component&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.880
of his fitness program. He consistently&nbsp;
took two or three days off each week.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:17.120
Many people think that they need to push&nbsp;
themselves to work out without taking a day off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:20.800
if they want to bulk up or lose weight,&nbsp;
but having scheduled rest days so that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:24.720
your muscles can heal is actually&nbsp;
crucial. Roberts definitely wanted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.880
Nanjiani to commit to a rigorous workout&nbsp;
schedule, but as a professional trainer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:33.280
he also understood that regular rest days&nbsp;
would be the key to long-term success.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:37.920
Spending time relaxing outside of the gym is&nbsp;
just as important as spending time in the gym!

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:44.000
They say that abs are made in the kitchen, and&nbsp;
this was definitely true for Nanjiani. Getting fit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.000
wasn't just about burning calories in the&nbsp;
gym — he also had to ensure that he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.160
fueling his body with healthy foods.&nbsp;
Sure, you can technically lose weight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:57.120
while eating sugary desserts or savory comfort&nbsp;
foods, but when it comes to building muscle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.360
you need to start with the right building&nbsp;
blocks and put nutritious foods on your plate.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:06.080
What was included in Nanjiani's food pyramid? He&nbsp;
went with the low-carb approach to dieting. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:10.640
also made sure to eat plenty of protein, which&nbsp;
is essential for building muscle and having a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:16.160
sustained source of energy for workouts. Nanjiani&nbsp;
also focused on adding healthy fats to his diet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:20.480
particularly sources of omega-3 fatty&nbsp;
acids. In addition, he made sure to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.720
drink plenty of water and stay hydrated.&nbsp;
If you're exercising as often as he was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.360
you don't want to forget your water&nbsp;
bottle when you go to the gym.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:33.360
Many people find that sticking to a consistent,&nbsp;
healthy diet is even more difficult than finding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:38.640
a form of exercise they enjoy. But for Kumail&nbsp;
Nanjiani, this wasn't the case. He was so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.720
dedicated to his fitness program that he&nbsp;
didn't want to take cheat days. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.480
one of the nutritionists he worked with&nbsp;
basically had to force him to take a day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:51.120
off from his diet and indulge every once in&nbsp;
a while. Nanjiani credits David Higgins for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:55.360
giving him permission to enjoy his favorite&nbsp;
foods and stop being so hard on himself.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:59.200
What did Nanjiani reach for on&nbsp;
cheat days? He grew up in Pakistan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.840
and he loves Pakistani food — but he admits&nbsp;
that this cuisine is very carb-heavy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:07.760
which meant that it wasn't appropriate for&nbsp;
his usual meal planning. But he says that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:13.200
traditional Pakistani food, like biryani, naan&nbsp;
bread, and rice, was his, quote, "go-to cheat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.680
meal" — and he would often feel so full after&nbsp;
eating it that he had to take a nap afterward.

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:23.040
When Roberts designed Nanjiani's workout&nbsp;
program, he had a philosophy in mind:

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:24.240
"No weak spots."

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:28.960
Yes, they would target certain muscles, but&nbsp;
overall, he wanted to create full-body workouts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:33.600
His goal? Help Nanjiani look like a real&nbsp;
bodybuilder. He encouraged Nanjiani to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:38.160
concentrate on "the symmetry of the musculature"&nbsp;
so that he would see improvements all over.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:41.840
Roberts admits that he pushed Nanjiani&nbsp;
in a way that he had never been pushed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:45.440
before — but Nanjiani was always&nbsp;
up for the challenge. Roberts says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:50.240
that Nanjiani was genuinely enthusiastic&nbsp;
about getting fit, telling Men's Journal,

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.560
"I was excited to work with Kumail because I&nbsp;
could tell he was ready to dedicate himself to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:58.560
the process. I have literally thousands&nbsp;
of text messages to prove that point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:01.840
Getting these kinds of results [doesn't]&nbsp;
happen without maximum effort."

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:06.880
When it comes to helping his clients, Roberts&nbsp;
clearly likes to stay on the cutting edge and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:12.080
utilize new technology in the world of fitness.&nbsp;
While working with Nanjiani, Roberts regularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:17.280
used electric stimulation, or e-stim, to&nbsp;
target certain muscles. Your average gym-goer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:21.760
may not have used this tool, but apparently&nbsp;
celebrity trainers like Roberts are big fans.

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:25.680
So, how does electric stimulation&nbsp;
work? Basically, Roberts would place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:31.040
pads hooked up to electric wires on Nanjiani's&nbsp;
back over specific muscle groups. Sometimes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:35.920
he would deliver a zap, which helped quote&nbsp;
"fire up" the muscles. It may sound strange,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:40.480
but Roberts is a fan of using this method with&nbsp;
clients. He used electric stimulation with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:43.120
Nanjiani about twice per week.
 

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:47.680
When you start working out and eating healthy, you&nbsp;
don't see results overnight. The waiting game is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:52.080
frustrating, but it takes a while to notice the&nbsp;
results you really want. However, according to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:57.600
Roberts, Nanjiani really didn't have to wait long&nbsp;
to see results. This is because Roberts went right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:02.560
in with workouts that were focused on intensity&nbsp;
— packing lots of action into a short timeframe.

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:05.120
This leads to fast muscle&nbsp;
building and weight loss,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:09.440
which was probably quite motivating&nbsp;
for Nanjiani. Roberts told Page Six,

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:13.520
"Kumail responded very quickly — as most&nbsp;
people do — when introduced to training&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:19.840
that shocks the system, whether it be for fat loss&nbsp;
or muscle gain or — as in Kumail's case — both."

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:24.720
When Nanjiani started working out to get ready&nbsp;
for Eternals, he felt like he had spent years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:29.280
holding himself back from his full potential.&nbsp;
He had generally worked in comedy — he was best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:33.600
known for Silicon Valley and The Big Sick — but&nbsp;
he knew if he wanted to try something different,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:37.840
he would need to transform his physique.&nbsp;
He had no idea just how strong he could get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:40.880
because he had never tried to figure&nbsp;
out what his physical limits were.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:46.000
At one point he was getting so muscular that&nbsp;
Marvel told Roberts and Nanjiani to scale back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:50.720
and slow down a bit — apparently, he looked,&nbsp;
quote, "too big and too cut" for the role.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:54.960
Therefore, Roberts lightened up on Nanjiani's&nbsp;
workouts. This probably wasn't the kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:58.720
of feedback that Nanjiani expected from&nbsp;
the studio, but it had to be flattering.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:01.840
"How do you feel?” 

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:05.560
“Taller."

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:11.680
The key to seeing amazing results in the gym&nbsp;
isn't just physical exercise — it's also about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:16.640
your mindset. Kumail Nanjiani said that his&nbsp;
perspective and sheer level of concentration&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:20.720
on his goals were necessary to achieve&nbsp;
the look he wanted. He told Men's Health,

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:25.120
"When I'm exercising, I'm not thinking&nbsp;
about anything else. It's like meditation."

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:29.200
Nanjiani even admitted that some of his&nbsp;
friends were dismayed by his new attitude&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:34.240
towards working out. He says that at one point,&nbsp;
they essentially, quote, "staged an intervention"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:38.240
to get him out of the gym for a few days.&nbsp;
They were worried that his intense focus on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:42.480
working out would detract from his skills&nbsp;
as a comedian. Nanjiani knew that outlook&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:46.800
might affect his work on funnier projects,&nbsp;
but he said that in the end, he didn't care.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:48.320
"I'm kind of obsessed with it."

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:52.480
Being funny wasn't his only priority&nbsp;
anymore — he was ready for a major change,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:55.680
and he was willing to accept the&nbsp;
sacrifices that would come along with it.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:00.560
In order to achieve the results he really&nbsp;
wanted, Nanjiani's nutritionists basically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:04.960
had to micromanage his diet. He had to be&nbsp;
exceptionally careful about eating sugar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.440
and whenever he ate something&nbsp;
sweet, he had to give them a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:11.520
heads up so they could plan his meals&nbsp;
accordingly. Nanjiani told Men's Health,

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:14.240
"They were like, 'If you're going&nbsp;
to have a can of Coke today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:17.120
let us know in the morning so we&nbsp;
can adjust and account for it.'"

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:21.760
Although he was allowed to enjoy cheat days,&nbsp;
he soon found that after eating such a clean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:26.240
diet all week long, going on a sugar binge during&nbsp;
the weekends would hold him back when he returned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:31.200
to the gym. Nanjiani admitted that on one&nbsp;
particular occasion, he decided to indulge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:36.320
in sticky toffee pudding, but came to regret&nbsp;
it the next day, saying that he felt so, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:40.880
"off" that he had to endure "twelve hours of&nbsp;
physical pain." He eventually got so strict&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:45.600
with his sugar intake that he ended up going an&nbsp;
entire year without eating even a single brownie.

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:50.880
There's a common mistake that people make when&nbsp;
they begin working out: they try to go all out and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:55.920
adopt some extreme habits, which inevitably don't&nbsp;
stick. As a personal trainer, Roberts is well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.920 --> 00:09:01.040
aware of these pitfalls, and he was determined&nbsp;
to help Nanjiani avoid them. Instead, Roberts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:06.240
made sure that Nanjiani was developing habits that&nbsp;
would be sustainable in the long-term, even after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:10.880
he dialed back on his original, intense training&nbsp;
schedule. Roberts told The Hollywood Reporter,

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:14.400
"We sent him away in peak physical&nbsp;
condition, but he's had to maintain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:18.240
that. I give him kudos for being able to&nbsp;
do that, especially when he was working."

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:22.720
It looks like the new Nanjiani is here to stay&nbsp;
— he's come a long way throughout this journey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:26.720
and there's no doubt that his skills will&nbsp;
impress audiences when Eternals premieres.

